{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"content_hash":"087d679e636e08063ee24ae523a193d831c5eb83530e7e4d4788bba6748c3e31","digest":{"component_or_area":"Reconciler JQL fetcher","key_entities":["fetcher.py","jql_active","jql_done_recent","statusCategory","status != Done","tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/test_fetch_multi_project.py","tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/test_fetch_paging_split.py"],"problem_keywords":["reconciler","active set scoping","status category","jql query","workflow agnostic","done equivalent"],"propositions":["jql_active hardcodes status != \"Done\" which fails to exclude custom closed-equivalent statuses (Closed, Resolved, Cancelled) that client workflows use, causing resolved issues to be incorrectly pulled into the active working set.","jql_done_recent uses literal status = \"Done\" and misses issues in custom Done-category statuses, so recent-resolved snapshots are incomplete for non-standard workflows.","Switching from literal status predicates to statusCategory = Done / statusCategory != Done makes the active/done scoping workflow-agnostic and compatible with all Jira workflows.","Single-project and multi-project fan-out logic and per-project scoping remain unchanged; DIG/REB workflows (using only To Do/In Progress/Done) produce identical behavior."]},"digest_hash_version":1,"model":"bedrock:us.anthropic.claude-opus-4-8","schema":"ticket_digest_v1"},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"TICKET_DIGEST","timestamp":1787316588435792001,"uuid":"e40e66f0-46c6-4720-850f-f32ffa094872"}